# `_shared/_md/` — the working text of our own assets

Every convertible asset under `_shared/` gets markdown here (eng-index-assets step 0, via
`convert_source.py`), for the same reason every source gets converted: **analysis reads the md
layer, page-level citation needs it (`<file>.md §Page N`), and reading binaries ad-hoc is what
the pack forbids everywhere else.** The binary stays as the evidence; the md is the text you
grep, cite and re-read without paying the extraction cost twice.

Files the converter cannot handle (a `.drawio` diagram, a helper script) stay original-only
and are noted in `firm_assets.md` §1b.

`convert_source.py --scan <root>` reports assets with no markdown here as `to CONVERT`.
This README is not a conversion manifest row — the converter registers each real conversion
below it.
